# Normalize line endings. Store text as LF in the repository AND check it out
# as LF in working trees on every platform, including Windows. This project's
# tooling assumes LF: gofmt rewrites to LF, and text/line processing in tests
# (e.g. the README-example extractor) splits on "\n". Without this, a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true produces CRLF working trees, which makes
# `gofmt -l` flag every file and previously broke a test.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Treat known binary artifacts as binary so git never applies EOL conversion
# or diffs them as text (these are normally build outputs and git-ignored, but
# be explicit in case one is ever force-added).
*.wasm  binary
*.gz    binary
*.br    binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
